<title>NETHERLANDS: EU jobs/growth deal seen Monday -French official.</title>
<headline>EU jobs/growth deal seen Monday -French official.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior French official said on Monday he expected a European Union summit to reach agreement by early Monday afternoon on a jobs and growth resolution and a budget stability pact.</p>
<p>The official, close to Prime Minister Lionel Jospin, told reporters: &quot;An agreement is probable at the end of the morning or in the early afternoon.&quot;</p>
<p>He said under the deal the European Investment Bank (EIB) would be allowed to support job creating programmes with soft loans.</p>
<p>Financing would come from the EIB's profits and would thus not require extra spending from member states.</p>
<p>However, he said that those funds would probably not be used to finance the major public works programmes known as Trans European Networks (TEN).</p>
</text>
